  "body": "In #3198, @foolip is working to remove the demo at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/2757de33552e6d9d0169e5a99c268db49e18b972#worker-used-for-background-i/o . I'd like to have some replacement for it.\r\n\r\nThis demo intends to demonstrate:\r\n\r\n- Using multiple workers on a page\r\n- Using a common library in multiple workers via importScripts, in this case to perform I/O (via sync XHR)\r\n- Using a worker to perform expensive operations that are not just numeric computation (the previous example takes care of numeric computation)\r\n- Interfacing with workers via postMessage/onmessage\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, it's not clear you need workers for the things this demo is doing. I/O is only expensive when you use sync XHR, which is bad anyway. You could create a similar demo using only the main thread plus non-sync XHR, or fetch.\r\n\r\nMaybe a community member can help us come up with a replacement that demonstrates similar things, but better, and doesn't rely on sync XHR. (Or CGI.)",
